settings.liquid:
{%- comment -%}
  Claude Code, 2026-08-30 - hero banner CSS for /pages/contact.

  TWO FIXES, both measured on the live page after the banner went up.

  1. DESKTOP RIGHT-PIN. The master is 3000x678 (4.425:1) and the box is a fixed
     440px height across a full-bleed width, so at 1440 the box is 3.27:1 and
     `cover` crops ~508px of width. Centred, half of that comes off the RIGHT,
     which is the side the clinician is on. Pinning right means the crop only ever
     removes extended backdrop.

  2. MOBILE TOP SCRIM. The mobile master is a face crop and her head reaches the
     top edge of the frame, so there is no dark band for the heading to sit on -
     measured, every 780px-wide window containing her face reads p95 144 / max 215
     in its top 12%. Padding graphite above her would mean inventing the crown of
     her head, which this pipeline does not do. So contrast is bought with a LOCAL
     scrim behind the type, never by raising the section overlay - a flatter
     overlay dims her face to fix the heading, which is the trade this project has
     already rejected once.

  Scoped with {{ section.id }} rather than the section class: the class would also
  match any other image-with-text-overlay that later lands on this template.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
@media screen and (min-width: 700px) {
  #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .content-over-media > picture > img,
  #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .content-over-media > img { object-position: right center; }
}

@media screen and (max-width: 699px) {
  #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .content-over-media::before {
    background-image: linear-gradient(to bottom, rgba(26, 26, 26, 0.88) 0%, rgba(26, 26, 26, 0.66) 26%, rgba(26, 26, 26, 0.00) 62%);
  }
}

/* The theme wraps a liquid block in a plain <div>, which takes a gap in the text
   stack and pushes the heading off centre. The style inside still applies while
   its wrapper is display:none. */
#shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .prose > div:has(> style) { display: none; }
</style>
<style>
/* Claude Code, 2026-08-31 - reduce the /pages/contact banner height.

   Malcolm asked for a shorter header banner. A plain smaller pixel height is the
   wrong tool HERE, because this master has no headroom: at the current 440px box
   and a 1920 viewport the crown of her head already sits ON the top edge. Dropping
   the box to a fixed 360px makes the box 5.33:1 against a 4.43:1 master, so cover
   crops 17% off the image HEIGHT and takes the top of her head with it. Rendered
   and looked at, not merely calculated - the clipping is visible.

   So the height is driven by the master's own ratio instead. The box then matches
   the picture at every desktop width and the crop stays at 0.1%, while still being
   markedly shorter: 341px at 1512 against the 440px it was, and 433px at 1920.
   The 280px floor keeps the heading room if the window is ever very narrow while
   still above the 700px breakpoint.

   Mobile is deliberately NOT reduced. Below 700px a different master is served -
   a face crop at 0.944:1 in a 1.040:1 box, so it is already cropped 9% vertically
   with her head against the top edge, which is why the mobile scrim above exists.
   Shortening that box clips her for real. */
@media screen and (min-width: 700px) {
  #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .content-over-media {
    --content-over-media-height: max(280px, calc(100vw / 4.43));
  }
}
</style>
